[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/banner.jpg[/img]

Homemade 1993 electric vehicles for [b]Dazed Power[/b] on [b]Build 42[/b]. Convert your car, rebuild a golf cart, work the yard with a garden tractor, fill the pack with batteries and charge it from your wired Dazed Power system or the sun. This is a [b]test build[/b]: all of it is built, much of it not yet tested in game.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] 1.7.0 or later and [b]Dazed Power[/b] (subscribe to both)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Built for it, server is the authority. Not tested on a server yet[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes, found vehicles spawn in unexplored areas[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Status[/b][/td][td]Test build, version 0.1.0[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedPowerEV[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-build.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/vehicles.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Club Cart[/b] and [b]Four-Seat Club Cart[/b]: found at well-off houses, trailer parks, farms and junkyards, or built.
[*][b]Elec-Trak[/b] garden tractor: found on farms, takes implements.
[*][b]Wedge Car[/b]: a homemade 60 km/h two-seater on a stripped Dart or Horizon.
[*][b]Ride-On ATV[/b]: a kids' battery quad on a pipe frame, fits through doors.
[*][b]Five-Wheel Utility Hauler[/b]: a rare find with a tipping bed.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/conversions.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Garage Conversion[/b]: right-click one of the seven donor cars from outside and pick [b]Convert to electric[/b]. 10 battery slots, about three quarters of the donor's speed.
[*]It becomes its own silent electric car (90 versions, police cars, taxis and work vans included) and keeps its paint, parts, contents and key.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-building.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/building.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Five magazines: [i]Convert It![/i] (the conversion, better chargers and arrays, battery trailer), [i]Golf Cart Rebuild[/i], [i]Build Your Own Commuter Car[/i], [i]Kid Kart Hacks[/i] and the [i]Electric Tractor Owner's Manual[/i].
[*]Everyone knows the makeshift battery, charger and roof array, the utility trailer, battery box, cell meter and balancer.
[*]Built vehicles roll out with an empty battery tray.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-pack.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/pack.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Car batteries (720 Wh), makeshift batteries (240 Wh, 12 torch batteries) and heavy deep-cycle batteries (1,400 Wh, last three times as long). Mix them freely; each keeps its own charge and health.
[*]An [b]insulated battery box[/b] halves the cold's range loss. A [b]pack balancer[/b] evens out the batteries on charge. A [b]cell meter[/b] reads every battery and flags the weak one.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-driving.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/driving.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Driving uses charge by distance, more flat out. Lights and heater draw too. Cold cuts range. Below 15% it limps, below 5% it crawls, flat it stalls.
[*]A Dazed Power-style dash shows charge, motor power and heat, range from how you really drive, and warning lamps.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-charging.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/charging.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build an [b]EV charger[/b] (Makeshift 600 W, Salvaged 1,200 W, Workshop 2,400 W), wire it in like the charging bench, park within 4 tiles and [b]Plug in charging lead[/b].
[*]Any other wired Dazed Power part within 10 tiles works as a 600 W lead. The dash shows the time to full.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-solar.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/solar.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Makeshift and Salvaged roof arrays fit the club carts, the wedge car and conversions. The Fold-Out array (wedge car and conversions) unfolds to three times the area when parked.
[*]They use Dazed Power's solar maths and charge while you drive.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-towing.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/towing.png[/img]
[list]
[*]The Elec-Trak's [b]mower deck[/b] cuts grass, the [b]furrow plough[/b] digs vanilla furrows (Dazed Dank crops work too) and the [b]front blade[/b] clears glass and rubble. Lower one and drive at 8 km/h or slower.
[*]Trailers: [b]utility[/b], [b]dump[/b] (tips its load) and [b]battery[/b] (six slots that join the towing EV's pack). Every EV has a hitch.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-faults.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/faults.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Motors heat up under load. Past 100 °C they ease off, and at 130 °C they cut out until they cool.
[*]Rare faults (main fuse, contactor, worn brushes) are mended from [b]Battery pack > Repair motor[/b].
[*]No idle, just a rising whine. Zombies hear each vehicle at its own loudness.
[*]Strip worn-out junkyard EVs for their motor and controller.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-planned.png[/img]
Planned: four-seat conversions trading the back seat for batteries, makeshift batteries in Dazed Power's banks, and a range-extender trailer. Plans can change.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only. Needs [b]Dazed Core[/b] 1.7.0+ and [b]Dazed Power[/b].
[*]Conversions are for the vanilla cars above. Burnt and smashed wrecks can't be converted.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/PowerEV/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, which vehicle, and your console.txt if there is an error.

